        "timestamp": 1786393937
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> alexcrichton submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14113#pullrequestreview-4900755996\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 615716559,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1786395892
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14113#discussion_r3753174311\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'm a bit wary of doing this even though it probably works out generally fine, but for example with guest-debug enabled I'd be worried that we'd spill/reload something or something like that. Could the payload here be directly on <code>FactInlineIntrinsic::Trap</code>? That'd require adding it to <code>Trampoline::Trap</code> too which I suspect wouldn't have much impact.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 615716561,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1786395893
